=head1 NAME

_SEPARATE_RECEPTORS_ - Separate input files by receptor

=head1 DESCRIPTION

This primitive groups the receptors in each input file according
to the "GROUP_BY" recpar (receptor name or polarization).
It is then split into a number of separate files using
"timesort" with a receptor list parameter.

The OCS config. XML is used to determine the total number
of spectral windows used in the observation.

The identifying information of files is updated as follows:

=over 4

=item SPECID and SUBSYSNR

Offset by the number of spectral windows for each group.

=over 4

=item SPECID

Used to control grouping of files into frames.

(See ORAC::Frame::ACSIS::framegroupkeys.)

=item SUBSYSNR

Modified to ensure group products have different file names,
and raw files are renamed to include this subsysten number to avoid confusion.

(See ORAC::Frame::ACSIS::file_from_bits_extra and ORAC::Group::ACSIS::file_from_bits.
file_from_bits_extra is also included in the group names shown in the log output
-- see ORAC::Core::orac_store_frm_in_correct_grp and ORAC::Group::name.)

=back

=item DRGROUP

A grouping key is added to the end of the current group name
in order to control grouping of frames.

(See ORAC::Frame::JCMT::findgroup.)

=back

